{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>After he had smitten.</b> Moses said: If I reprove them before they enter the border of the land, they will say — what is this upon us? What good has he done us? He comes only to pick a quarrel and find a pretext, that he has no strength to bring us into the land. Therefore he waited until he had struck down Sihon and Og before them and dispossessed them of their land, and after that he reprove them. (Sifrei)" "<b>Sihon, who dwelt in Heshbon.</b> If Sihon had not been fierce and had been dwelling in Heshbon — it would have been hard, for the province is hard. And if it had been another city and Sihon dwelling in it — it would have been hard, for the king is fierce. How much more so, since the king is fierce and the province is hard. (ibid.)" "<b>who dwelt in Ashtaroth.</b> The king is fierce and the province is hard." "<b>Ashtaroth.</b> It is an expression of pressure and hardness, like ״עַשְׁתְּרֹת קַרְנַיִם״ (Genesis 14). And this Ashtaroth is Ashtaroth-karnaim, where there were Rephaim whom Amraphel smote, as it says (ibid.) ״וַיַּכּוּ אֶת רְפָאִים בְּעַשְׁתְּרֹת קַרְנַיִם״. And Og survived from them, as it says (ibid.) ״וַיָּבֹא הַפָּלִיט״, and it says (Deuteronomy 3) ״כִּי רַק עוֹג מֶלֶךְ הַבָּשָׁן נִשְׁאַר מִיֶּתֶר הָרְפָאִים״." "<b>In Edrei.</b> The name of the kingdom."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:45:24.187065914Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}